          "message": "feat(vectors): recall-gated ANN index for concept dedup + k-NN (#2251) [FABLE-5] (#2256)\n\nAdd build_ann / knn / dedup to sparq-vectors behind the existing opt-in\napprox-ann feature — the surface sparq issue #2251 requests for the\nKernel-of-Truth scale track (cross-source concept dedup past the ~100k rung,\nwhere exact O(m^2) dedup is intractable).\n\n- build_ann(vectors, policy) -> ConceptAnnIndex: HNSW (the crate's existing\n  instant-distance backend, same Arc-backed normalised point type as\n  VectorIndex) over raw (id, vector) pairs — no Graph/VectorStore needed.\n  Fail-closed input validation. No new dependency.\n- knn(index, q, k) (free fn + method; knn_of by indexed id): APPROXIMATE\n  cosine top-k, recall < 1.0.\n- dedup(index, policy, exact_ground_truth) -> DedupReport: the RECALL GATE\n  runs first (set-based recall@k vs the exact O(m^2) oracle); below\n  policy.recall_gate (default 0.99) it returns Err and NO merge is computed\n  (fail-closed). Only after the gate: above-threshold neighbour pairs ->\n  union-find groups -> (duplicate, canonical=smallest-id) merges.\n- exact_ground_truth / GroundTruth::new: the exact oracle builder + a wrapper\n  for an externally-computed oracle, with malformed-oracle validation.\n\ntests/dedup.rs pins both halves of the gate: recall >= 0.99 vs an in-test\nexact ground truth (merges emitted only then), and Err+no-merge below the\ngate; plus planted-near-duplicate merge semantics and the fail-closed matrix.\n\nDocs updated same change (MAINTENANCE RULE): skills/vector-search/SKILL.md\n(frontmatter, Key APIs, recipe 22, approx-ann gotcha) and the crate README\n(Features bullet, kept at the 120-line template cap).\n\nGates: cargo test -p sparq-vectors green in BOTH feature states; clippy\n--all-targets -D warnings both states; rustdoc --all-features -D warnings;\nprivacy-claims / no-perf-numbers / readme-template clean.\n\nRefs #2251.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
